e":"G6 T3 W12 - Complete the improvement - Words in use 2","spark_text":"We test the program by pressing the button three times. The feedback says to check the displayed total after a reset.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/test"},{"id":"grade6_t3_2026_w13_part1_spark","status":"archived"},{"id":"grade6_t3_2026_w13_part2_spark","status":"archived"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w02_part1_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W02 - Spreadsheet cells, charts and formulas - Words in use 1","spark_text":"Cell B3 contains the number of students in the club. The table puts each club name beside its student count. The formula =B2+B3 adds two cell values.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/cell"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w02_part2_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W02 - Spreadsheet cells, charts and formulas - Words in use 2","spark_text":"The function SUM adds a range of spreadsheet values. The chart uses bars to compare the club counts.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/function"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w03_part1_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W03 - Interpret charts and calculations - Words in use 1","spark_text":"The formula =B2+B3 adds two cell values. The total is the number of bottles collected by all teams. The average for 10, 20 and 30 is 20.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/formula"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w03_part2_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W03 - Interpret charts and calculations - Words in use 2","spark_text":"The chart uses bars to compare the club counts. Our comparison shows that chess has more students than art.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/chart"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w04_part1_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W04 - Scratch delivery practice - Words in use 1","spark_text":"The deliver function moves the sprite and adds one delivery. The loop repeats the delivery three times. The variable count stores the number of button presses.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/function"},{"id":"grade7_t3_2026_w04_part2_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G7 T3 W04 - Scratch delivery practice - Words in use 2","spark_text":"The sprite starts at position x equals zero. Click the green flag to reset the sprite and delivery count.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary exam