y_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Scripting/Events"},{"id":"grade8_t3_2026_w09_part2_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G8 T3 W09 - Scratch controls - Words in use 2","spark_text":"The displayed number is an output from the counter. The bug makes the app show the wrong lunch choice.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/output"},{"id":"grade8_t3_2026_w10_part1_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G8 T3 W10 - Scratch game rules - Words in use 1","spark_text":"The Player sprite moves when the arrow key is pressed. A button click is an event that starts the instructions. The loop repeats the delivery three times.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://techterms.com/definition/sprite"},{"id":"grade8_t3_2026_w10_part2_spark","status":"scheduled","title":"G8 T3 W10 - Scratch game rules - Words in use 2","spark_text":"The condition checks whether the distance is greater than 18. The variable count stores the number of button presses.","why_it_matters":"Use these words to explain what happens in this week\u2019s Technology work.","question":"Choose one example. Explain what its vocabulary word means in that situation.","source_title":"Weekly Technology vocabulary examples","source_url":"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dic